# Desktop dialect

The UI source of truth is `%USERPROFILE%\Documents\Widgets\desktop\index.html` (this repo ships a copy under `templates/starter/`).

## Pieces

- `.widget` — static tile on the canvas (`article`)
- `.spawnable` — template; host opens a native always-on-top window
- `.action-bar` — optional class on a spawnable (example command bar, not a host window type)

Required on the opening tag: `data-id`. Optional: `data-w`, `data-h`, `data-anchor`, `data-hooks`, `data-hotkey`.

`data-hooks` is a comma list from: `media`, `mouse`, `layout`, `spawn`, `shell`, `hotkey`, `pty`. The host never grants more than that list. `calc` aliases `calculator`.

`data-anchor="c"` (or `center` / `overlay`) = centered overlay with dim. `tr` = docked slide-out.

The first spawnable with the `hotkey` hook is what Alt+Space toggles. Engine/JS for an example bar lives in the page (`desktop/bar.js`), not the host.

Host knobs and shortcuts: `<script type="application/json" id="versailles">` in the same HTML file. Runtime (token, session, desktop shown) stays in `.versailles/`.

## Do not

- Do not iframe per-widget HTML.
- Do not add a settings UI to the action bar.
- Preview with `?m=desktop|widgets|spawn|spawn&id=…|action_bar`.
